Session servers: a socket prefix of this app's own.

Each session's server listens on /var/tmp/<prefix><pid>. At launch, the
app adopts every orphaned server whose socket has its prefix: that is
how sessions survive a crash. With upstream's prefix ("iTerm2.socket."),
this app would adopt the sessions upstream iTerm2 left behind, and
upstream would adopt this app's. The prefix is now
"Mavericks-iTerm2.socket.". The server and the adopter share the one
constant.

--- a/sources/iTermFileDescriptorSocketPath.c
+++ b/sources/iTermFileDescriptorSocketPath.c
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
-const char *iTermFileDescriptorSocketNamePrefix = "iTerm2.socket.";
+const char *iTermFileDescriptorSocketNamePrefix = "Mavericks-iTerm2.socket.";
 
 
 // From http://apple.stackexchange.com/questions/22694/private-tmp-vs-private-var-tmp-vs-tmpdir
